Server Information
==================

This folder contains templates for hosting Zine through standard Python web
server interfaces.  Install Zine into the server's Python environment, copy
the appropriate template, and set ``INSTANCE_FOLDER`` (or the
``ZINE_INSTANCE`` environment variable) to a writable instance directory.

``zine.wsgi``
    A WSGI module for mod_wsgi or another server that imports an
    ``application`` callable.

``zine.fcgi``
    A FastCGI executable. Install Zine with the ``fastcgi`` extra to provide
    its flup6 dependency. FastCGI is retained for compatible legacy hosting.

``zine.cgi``
    A standard-library CGI executable. CGI starts Zine for every request and
    performs poorly, so it should only be used when no persistent WSGI option
    is available.

The templates retain process-wide database pool overrides.  Set
``POOL_SIZE``, ``POOL_RECYCLE``, or ``POOL_TIMEOUT`` in a copied template, or
set the corresponding ``ZINE_DATABASE_POOL_*`` environment variables (the
historical ``ZINE_POOL_*`` names are also accepted).  Only enable
``BEHIND_PROXY`` / ``ZINE_BEHIND_PROXY`` for requests from a trusted proxy.
